Time Complexity:
O((m × n) × (m + n))

Space Complexity:
O(m × n)

Approach:
1. Create a temporary matrix and copy all elements from the original matrix
2. Traverse the original matrix
3. Whenever a cell containing 0 is found, set its entire row to 0 in the temporary matrix
4. Also set its entire column to 0 in the temporary matrix
5. After processing all zeroes, copy the temporary matrix back to the original matrix
6. The original matrix is updated with the required zeroes




class Solution {
    public void setZeroes(int[][] matrix) {
        int m = matrix.length;
        int n = matrix[0].length;
        int temp[][] = new int[m][n];

        for(int i=0; i<m; i++){
            for(int j=0; j<n; j++){
                temp[i][j] = matrix[i][j];
            }
        }

        for(int i=0; i<m; i++){
            for(int j=0; j<n; j++){
                if(matrix[i][j] == 0){
                    for(int k=0; k<m; k++){
                        temp[k][j] = 0;
                    }
                    for(int l=0; l<n; l++){
                        temp[i][l] = 0;
                    }
                }
            }
        }

        for(int i=0; i<m; i++){
            for(int j=0; j<n; j++){
                matrix[i][j] = temp[i][j];
            }
        }
    }
}
